      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Endoscopy and ultrasound was used to diagnose a 13 year old virgin girl who presented with dysmenorrhoea and suspected right side adnexal tumescence. The girl was found to have a complete septate uterus with non-communicating right hemicavity and haematometra, an exceptional type of Müllerian anomaly. After pretreatment with buserelin, hysteroscopic metroplasty was successfully performed."},
